<p>Today I learned about <a href="https://quxnet.net/">quxnet</a> via the always interesting <a href="https://82mhz.net/posts/2026/10/linkdump-no-130/">Linkdump, from 82MHz</a>, who linked to <a href="https://moddedbear.com/quxnet-is-a-breath-of-fresh-air">Quxnet Is a Breath of Fresh Air | moddedbear.com</a>. Of course I created an account immediately  because how could I not? I mean, there's an SSH/TUI interface for it. Sold!</p>
<p><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20261023-quxnet-tui.png" alt="" /></p>
<p>Quxnet has everything. Boards, mail, photo galleries, links, blogs, an RSS reader, and more. It looks super-retro cool, which adds to the vibe. I don't know what I want out of it yet, but if it can remain &quot;A private network with old internet manners.&quot; then I can see it becoming a fun new place to hang out.</p>
<p>There are still fewer than 1,000 people there, so naturally things are cordial and sufficiently nerdy and polite. I hope it stays polite, but I worry that with popularity comes conflicting views from people who &quot;We&quot; don't agree with, and once the finger-pointing starts, things tend to go south. I hope it doesn't happen that way.</p>
<p>But for now it's clever, fun, nerdy, and new, so I'm in. https://quxnet.net/u/jbaty.</p>
